<article class="env-lemma" id="0BP0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BP0">Lemma <span data-tag="0BP0">15.92.14</span>.</a> Let $(R \to R',f)$ be a glueing pair. Then $\text{Tor}^ R_1(R', R/R[f^\infty ]) = 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have $R/R[f^\infty ] = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits R/R[f^ n] = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits f^ nR$. As formation of Tor groups commutes with filtered colimits (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BNF" data-tag="0BNF">10.76.2</a>) we may apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0BNZ" data-tag="0BNZ">15.92.13</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>